==========================================================================
STEP 5: load distribution over the three servers (round-robin baseline)
==========================================================================
  Before each request the VIP rule is re-pointed at the next server, so
  the traffic really goes h2, h3, h4, h2, h3, h4 ...  The client always
  asks for the same VIP; only the switch rule changes.
  OK   distribution rule->h2  served_by=h2      1.8 ms
  OK   distribution rule->h3  served_by=h3      1.7 ms
  OK   distribution rule->h4  served_by=h4      1.7 ms
  OK   distribution rule->h2  served_by=h2      1.5 ms
  OK   distribution rule->h3  served_by=h3      6.4 ms
  OK   distribution rule->h4  served_by=h4      1.6 ms
  OK   distribution rule->h2  served_by=h2      1.7 ms
  OK   distribution rule->h3  served_by=h3      1.7 ms
  OK   distribution rule->h4  served_by=h4      1.6 ms
  --- OpenFlow rules currently in s1 (after distribution) ---
